{"id":"CVE-2026-129491","published":"2026-11-16T01:17:18.857Z","modified":"2026-11-16T01:17:18.857Z","status":"Received","description":"Qbian61 forum-java commit 20f7e68 through commit 63152c4 contains a stored cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows authenticated users to inject script by posting unsanitized comment content rendered via jQuery .html() in the reply dialog. Attackers can post comments with img onerror payloads that execute when victims click Reply, stealing the non-HttpOnly sid session cookie to hijack accounts including administrators.","products":["Qbian61 / forum-java"],"score":5.1,"cvssVersion":"4.0","scoreSource":"disclosure@vulncheck.com","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","weaknesses":["CWE-79"],"references":["https://github.com/Qbian61/forum-java/blob/63152c49c71ad8121bda6e9a03a7ba7dc39ae52c/forum-portal/src/main/resources/templates/include/comment-list.html#L56-L60","https://github.com/Qbian61/forum-java/blob/63152c49c71ad8121bda6e9a03a7ba7dc39ae52c/forum-portal/src/main/resources/templates/include/posts-script.html#L30-L34","https://github.com/Qbian61/forum-java/issues/25","https://vul.yulun.ac.cn/20261115/forum-java/","https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/qbian61-forum-java-commit-20f7e68-through-63152c4-stored-xss-via-comment-reply-dialog"]}
{"id":"CVE-2026-129492","published":"2026-11-16T01:17:19.737Z","modified":"2026-11-16T01:17:19.737Z","status":"Received","description":"Bolo (bolo-solo) 1.7 through 2.6.4 contains a stored cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to inject scripts via the unsanitized commentOriginalCommentName parameter. Attackers can post a comment to /article/comments with a short payload that steals non-HttpOnly session cookies from visitors, enabling takeover of administrator accounts.","products":["bolo-blog / bolo-solo"],"score":5.3,"cvssVersion":"4.0","scoreSource":"disclosure@vulncheck.com","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","weaknesses":["CWE-79"],"references":["https://github.com/bolo-blog/bolo-solo/blob/e0ab6b1f57a4ba66b4a42a7b6ceafb87c33290cc/src/main/java/org/b3log/solo/service/CommentMgmtService.java#L299-L306","https://github.com/bolo-blog/bolo-solo/blob/e0ab6b1f57a4ba66b4a42a7b6ceafb87c33290cc/src/main/webapp/skins/bolo-nexmoe/common-comment.ftl#L29-L34","https://github.com/bolo-blog/bolo-solo/issues/331","https://vul.yulun.ac.cn/20261115/bolo-solo/","https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bolo-bolo-solo-1.7-through-2.6.4-stored-xss-via-comment-reply-to-name"]}
{"id":"CVE-2026-129493","published":"2026-11-16T01:17:19.897Z","modified":"2026-11-16T01:17:19.897Z","status":"Received","description":"Bolo (bolo-solo) 1.7 through 2.6.4 contains an information disclosure vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to read article view passwords via the public GET /articles endpoint. Attackers can retrieve the plaintext articleViewPwd field returned by ArticleProcessor.getArticlesByPage and submit it to read password-protected article content.","products":["bolo-blog / bolo-solo"],"score":8.7,"cvssVersion":"4.0","scoreSource":"disclosure@vulncheck.com","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","weaknesses":["CWE-201"],"references":["https://github.com/bolo-blog/bolo-solo/blob/e0ab6b1f57a4ba66b4a42a7b6ceafb87c33290cc/src/main/java/org/b3log/solo/processor/ArticleProcessor.java#L442-L478","https://github.com/bolo-blog/bolo-solo/issues/331","https://vul.yulun.ac.cn/20261115/bolo-solo/","https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bolo-bolo-solo-1.7-through-2.6.4-article-password-disclosure-via-articles"]}
{"id":"CVE-2026-129494","published":"2026-11-16T01:17:20.053Z","modified":"2026-11-16T01:17:20.053Z","status":"Received","description":"CloudPaste 1.1.0 through 1.9.1 contains an information disclosure vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to obtain WebDAV storage credentials through the unauthenticated /api/proxy/link endpoint. Attackers who know a public share slug can retrieve the Basic Authorization header containing the WebDAV username and password, then read, modify, or delete files on the WebDAV server.","products":["ling-drag0n / CloudPaste"],"score":8.7,"cvssVersion":"4.0","scoreSource":"disclosure@vulncheck.com","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","weaknesses":["CWE-522"],"references":["https://github.com/ling-drag0n/CloudPaste/blob/282ea1c7fbbcd4fab40527664bf7479fd5bb922d/backend/src/routes/proxyLinkRoutes.js#L139-L167","https://github.com/ling-drag0n/CloudPaste/blob/282ea1c7fbbcd4fab40527664bf7479fd5bb922d/backend/src/storage/drivers/webdav/WebDavStorageDriver.js#L800-L819","https://github.com/ling-drag0n/CloudPaste/issues/223","https://vul.yulun.ac.cn/20261115/cloudpaste/","https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/cloudpaste-1.1.0-through-1.9.1-webdav-credential-disclosure-via-api-proxy-link"]}
